  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/nh-rsa-data/blob/96bd0a247d4463e2ae692310c0fdd17ec563a46c/rsa_html/VII/105/105-6.htm",
  "statuteText": "105:6 Police Regulations. –\n\nThe police officers of a town may make regulations for the stand of hacks, drays, public automobiles, and carts, in any street, lane, or alley; for the height and position of any awning, shade, or fixture in front of or near a building; and respecting any obstruction in any street, lane, or alley, or in any stable or other outbuilding."
